  "question": {
    "text": "The area bounded by the $x$ -axis, the curve $y=f(x)$ and the lines $\\mathrm{x}=1, \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{b},$ is equal to $\\sqrt{\\mathrm{b}^{2}+1}-\\sqrt{2}$\r\n\r\nfor all $b>1,$ then $f(x)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "yUcxM",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{x-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JsLdt",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{x+1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QI8nu",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kny0N",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+x^{2}}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\int_{1}^{\\mathrm{b}} \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}) \\mathrm{dx}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{b}^{2}+1}-\\sqrt{2}$\r\n\r\nDifferentiate with respect to $\\mathrm{b}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nf(b)=\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{b^{2}+1}} \\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}\r\n\r\n$$",
